hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22307","Ismail ibn Muhammad, and he is Abu Ibrahim al-Muaqqib, narrated to us, Marwan, meaning ibn Muawiyah al-Fazari, narrated to us, Mansur ibn Hayyan al-Asadi narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bishr al-Khuzai, from his maternal uncle Malik ibn Abdullah, he said: I campaigned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I did not pray behind an imam whose prayer was briefer than his, with completeness of bowing and prostration."
"22308","Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, ibn Jabir narrated to us, that Abu al-Musabbih al-Awzai narrated to them, he said: While we were traveling on the pass of Qalamiyyah, a man leading his horse on the mountainside called to the commander Malik ibn Abdullah al-Khathami: O Abu Abdullah, will you not ride? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever his two feet become dusty in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, for an hour of the day, they are forbidden to the Fire."
"22309","Waki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Shuaythi narrated to us, from Layth ibn al-Mutawakkil, from Malik ibn Abdullah al-Khathami, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever his two feet become dusty in the path of Allah, Allah has forbidden him to the Fire."
"22310","Affan narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Mansur ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Sulayman al-Khuzai narrated to me, from his maternal uncle Malik ibn Abdullah, he said: I campaigned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I never prayed behind an imam leading the people whose prayer was lighter than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
